- op: discuss  # 3af8
  at: '2026-11-01T22:22:30Z'  # 3af8
  by: agent  # 3af8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3af8
  clock: 6  # 3af8
  nonce: 3af8  # 3af8
  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/ctrl1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. P4 review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f: `timeout --preserve-status -s INT 4 hypergumbo survey <copy of core/linkers> --out X.json` gave rc=130 and a 30-line traceback ending in concurrent/futures/_base.py as_completed -> threading wait -> KeyboardInterrupt, with no output file. `hypergumbo run` reproduces it the same way. Root-cause field correction: the top-level handler now EXISTS (WI-himas done, PR #546), but it deliberately catches Exception only, so Ctrl-C still escapes. The fix is one `except KeyboardInterrupt` branch there. MECHANISM: main()'s top-level handler (cli.py ~13919-13970, WI-himas) catches Exception, not BaseException; KeyboardInterrupt raised in as_completed() in run_all_analyzers (all_analyzers.py:476) propagates to the interpreter."  # 3af8
